#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:23
msgid "Cover tile size"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:24
msgid "Small is 150×225, medium 200×300 and large 250×375 pixels."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:32
msgid "Library layout"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:33
msgid ""
"Whether the desktop library shows its games as covers in a grid or as rows "
"in a list with their source, install state, last played date and playtime. "
"Fullscreen mode always shows the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:37
msgid "Exit after launching a store game"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:38
msgid ""
"Quit once a store game is handed to its launcher. Games Pindu launcher "
"starts itself keep it running, as it records their play sessions."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:42
msgid "Show badges on covers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:43
msgid "The launcher badge top left and the state badge top right."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:47
msgid "Sources left out of the sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:48
msgid "Source IDs whose sidebar rows are hidden; their games still import."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:52
msgid "Source order for a game's copies"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:53
msgid ""
"Source IDs, first preferred: which copy Play starts for a game with copies "
"from several sources when you chose none. Sources left out follow in the "
"default order."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:57
msgid "Prefer SteamGridDB art"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:58
msgid ""
"Show SteamGridDB art before the launcher's own; art you pick always comes "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:62
msgid "Get metadata from Wikidata"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:63
msgid ""
"Let Refresh Metadata look games up on Wikidata by their Steam app ID for "
"their developer and genres. Nothing is fetched until you ask, and never "
"during an import."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:67
msgid "Show titles below covers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:71
msgid "Navigate the window with a controller"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:72
msgid ""
"Move focus with the D-pad or left stick, open with A and go back with B. "
"Controllers are only opened while this is on."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:82
msgid "Button prompts"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:83
msgid ""
"The glyphs fullscreen mode shows for the controller's buttons. Auto follows "
"the controller: letters with A at the bottom, shapes, or letters with A on "
"the right. Steam Input shows every controller as its own virtual pad, which "
"Auto takes for letters."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:92
msgid "Swap confirm and back"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:93
msgid ""
"Whether the right face button confirms and the bottom one goes back, rather "
"than the other way round. Auto swaps them when the button prompts put A on "
"the right."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:97
msgid "Controller button bindings"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:98
msgid ""
"The fullscreen functions given to other controller buttons from the menu's "
"Controls: each changed button, such as north or left-shoulder, with its "
"function, such as search. Buttons not listed keep their default function. "
"Guide, the D-pad and the left stick never change."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:107
msgid "Navigation repeat delay"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:108
msgid ""
"How long a controller direction is held in fullscreen mode before focus "
"starts moving again on its own: short is 0.2 seconds, normal 0.3 and long "
"0.6. It changes only the launcher's own navigation, never what a game "
"receives."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:117
msgid "Navigation repeat rate"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:118
msgid ""
"How fast focus keeps moving while a controller direction is held in "
"fullscreen mode: slow is every 100 ms, normal every 50 ms and fast every 30 "
"ms. It changes only the launcher's own navigation, never what a game "
"receives."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:127
msgid "Stick dead zone for navigation"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:128
msgid ""
"How far the left stick moves before it moves focus in fullscreen mode: small "
"is past 30 % of its travel, normal past half and large past 70 %. It changes "
"only the launcher's own navigation, never what a game receives."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:132
msgid "Default Proton build"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:133
msgid ""
"The internal name of the Proton build Windows games run with unless they "
"name their own. Empty for the newest build on this computer."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:137
msgid "Prefix folder"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:138
msgid ""
"The folder new Windows games get their own prefix in. Empty for ~/Games/"
"pindu-launcher/prefixes."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:142
msgid "Folder for copies of save snapshots"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:143
msgid ""
"The folder, picked through the file chooser, that every new save snapshot is "
"also copied to, as the sandbox reaches it. Empty to keep snapshots only in ~/"
"Games/pindu-launcher/save-snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:147
msgid "Save folders added by hand"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:148
msgid ""
"The folders, picked through the file chooser, that a game's save snapshots "
"hold besides its prefix, by game ID, as the sandbox reaches them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:152
msgid "MangoHud for new Windows games"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:153
msgid ""
"Whether Windows games added from now on start with the MangoHud performance "
"overlay."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:157
msgid "GameMode for new Windows games"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:158
msgid "Whether Windows games added from now on start with GameMode."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:162
msgid "Start in fullscreen mode"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:163
msgid ""
"Open the window in fullscreen mode, the controller-driven presentation of "
"the library."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:167
msgid "Navigation sounds"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:168
msgid ""
"Play a soft sound in fullscreen mode when the controller moves focus, "
"selects or goes back."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:173
msgid "Navigation sound volume"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:174
msgid "How loud the navigation sounds play, from 0 (silent) to 100 (full)."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:178
msgid "Reduce motion in fullscreen mode"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:179
msgid ""
"Hold Home's animated background on its first frame and change art without a "
"crossfade in fullscreen mode. Turning off animations in the system settings "
"does the same."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:189
msgid "Text size in fullscreen mode"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:190
msgid ""
"How large fullscreen mode's text is, for reading from across the room: each "
"step past default adds about a quarter. The desktop window is not affected."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:194
msgid "Larger text in fullscreen mode (replaced)"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:195
msgid ""
"Replaced by fullscreen-text-size. On start-up, when this is on and no text "
"size is chosen yet, the text size becomes large, the size this gave, and "
"this turns off."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:199
msgid "Hold to confirm in fullscreen mode"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:200
msgid ""
"Make Power Off, Restart, Forget and Stop need the controller's confirm "
"button held down for a second in fullscreen mode, with the hold's progress "
"shown. The keyboard and the pointer act at once."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:204
msgid "Custom fullscreen style"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:205
msgid ""
"Restyle fullscreen mode with your own stylesheet, fullscreen.css in the "
"app's config folder. The desktop window is not affected."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:209
msgid "Fullscreen design"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:210
msgid ""
"The id of the design fullscreen mode is shown in: a theme folder shipped "
"with the app (Lobby by default) or in the app's config folder under themes. "
"Empty for Adwaita, the standard look. A design the app no longer ships "
"(Ribbon, Panorama) is replaced with Lobby. The desktop window is not "
"affected."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:214
msgid "Fullscreen design variant"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:215
msgid ""
"The id of the chosen variant of the fullscreen design, for a design that "
"offers variants; its stylesheet applies after the design's own. An empty or "
"unknown id picks the design's first variant."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:223
msgid "Fullscreen Home background"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:224
msgid "The animated background behind Home's first screen in fullscreen mode."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:233
msgid "Fullscreen background blur"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:234
msgid ""
"How much Home's background and the focused game's art behind it are blurred "
"in fullscreen mode. A design can restyle each strength."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:243
msgid "Fullscreen background dim"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:244
msgid ""
"How much Home's background and the focused game's art behind it are darkened "
"in fullscreen mode. A design can restyle each strength."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:248
msgid "SteamGridDB prompt shown"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:249
msgid ""
"Whether the window has offered, once, to set up a SteamGridDB API key for "
"game art."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:253
msgid "First sync summary shown"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:254
msgid ""
"Whether the summary of what the library's first sync found has been "
"dismissed, after which it never shows again."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:258
msgid "Last library backup"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.gschema.xml.in:259
msgid ""
"When the library was last exported, in seconds since the Unix epoch; 0 means "
"never. Library Health shows it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:8
msgid "Play all your games"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:10
msgid ""
"Pindu launcher gathers every game on your computer into one library, "
"whichever launcher installed it. Browse your covers, pick up where you left "
"off and start any game with one click."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:15
msgid "Games come from:"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid "Steam, native or Flatpak"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:18
msgid "Heroic: Epic Games, GOG, Amazon and sideloaded games"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:19
msgid "Lutris, Bottles, Faugus, Legendary and itch"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid "Games installed as apps, including Flatpaks"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:21
msgid "Games you add yourself"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid "Keep your library tidy:"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:25
msgid "Search, sort and filter by installed, favourite, Windows or native"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:26
#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:70
msgid "Group games into your own collections"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:27
msgid "Jump back into recent and pinned games"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:28
msgid ""
"See when you played and for how long, including playtime from your launchers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:29
msgid "Hide games you never play"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:30
msgid "Choose your own artwork, or find it on SteamGridDB with your own key"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:32
msgid ""
"Store games start through their own launcher, which keeps their settings, "
"updates and playtime. Your library works offline, and nothing leaves your "
"computer unless you ask for artwork."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:58
msgid "All your games in one library"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:62
msgid "Details and launch options for each game"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:66
msgid "See what you played and for how long"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:74
msgid "Light and dark style"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:92
msgid ""
"New fullscreen designs, copies of one game shown as one, save snapshots, "
"Library Health, richer game details, two new sources and much more of the "
"launcher in fullscreen mode."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:94
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode has three new designs: Lobby, now the default, with labelled "
"section tiles over the animated background; Marquee, which opens Home on "
"your recent games; and Shelves, every section as a row of its games. Ribbon "
"and Panorama are retired, and if you used either, fullscreen mode opens in "
"Lobby"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:95
msgid ""
"Adwaita, the look with no design, now follows GNOME Software's Explore page: "
"your recent games in a carousel with Play and Details, a row of sections, "
"then a row of covers for each; Quick Access is a floating card and the menu "
"drawer a plain sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:96
msgid ""
"Steam, Lutris, Bottles, Faugus, Legendary and itch show their own icons in "
"the sidebar, on covers and on fullscreen Home's tiles"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:97
msgid ""
"In Lobby, Quick Access lets you choose Home's background under Design: the "
"new Red Ribbons or Blue Station"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:98
msgid ""
"Rename a game, or set its developer, genres, release year and description, "
"in its Edit dialog; your changes survive every sync"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:99
msgid ""
"Steam games show their release year, genres, controller support and Steam "
"Deck rating, and Lutris and Heroic Amazon games their release year"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:100
msgid ""
"Get Metadata From Wikidata, off by default, fills in Steam games' developers "
"and genres on request, and the game page says which values came from Wikidata"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:101
msgid ""
"Filter the library by genre or to games never played, and save a filter as a "
"collection whose games follow it"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:102
msgid ""
"A list view beside the library grid, and a selection mode that favourites, "
"hides or adds many games to a collection at once, with Undo"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:103
msgid ""
"Copies of a game from several sources show as one game: Duplicates suggests "
"copies to group, you can merge and split games by hand, and Copy Order in "
"Preferences decides which copy Play starts"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:104
msgid ""
"A Windows game's saves are kept as a snapshot when it exits, can be restored "
"from Save Snapshots, and can also be copied to a folder you choose; any game "
"can have its save folders added by hand"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:105
msgid ""
"Library Health, in the main menu and in Quick Access, shows what needs "
"attention with a button for the next step, and the first sync ends with a "
"summary of what it found"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:106
msgid ""
"Preferences shows when each source last synced and the problems it ran into"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:107
msgid ""
"Games installed with the itch app or with the standalone Legendary command-"
"line tool join the library"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:108
msgid ""
"When a launch fails, the game page says why and offers the next step, and "
"Start Safely runs a game once without MangoHud, GameMode or its wrappers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:109
msgid "Steam games link to ProtonDB and PCGamingWiki"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:110
msgid ""
"About's Debugging Information holds a report for bug reports, which can "
"include a game's newest log; in fullscreen mode Quick Access shows it to "
"photograph and saves a copy"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:111
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode can add a game, turn sources on and off, take the "
"SteamGridDB key, download and remove Proton builds, choose a game's Proton "
"build, and rename, reorder and delete collections, all with a controller"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:112
msgid "The fullscreen game page shows a game's details and description"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:113
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode offers four text sizes, and Hold to Confirm makes Power Off, "
"Restart, Forget and Stop wait for a held button"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:114
msgid ""
"Quick Access sets the controller's repeat delay, repeat rate and stick dead "
"zone"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:115
msgid ""
"Under high contrast, fullscreen Home's background is still and plain, and "
"text over game art sits on darker shading"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:116
msgid ""
"Screen readers hear how many games match a search or filter, Play buttons "
"and check boxes are named after their game, and the game title and Jump Back "
"In are headings"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:117
msgid ""
"Tab leaves the library grid in one step, and the arrow keys move between "
"games"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:118
msgid ""
"Backups carry game groups, saved filters and the details you or a provider "
"set, and the launcher remembers when you last backed up"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:119
msgid ""
"The launcher keeps a copy of your library before it updates the library's "
"format"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:120
msgid "Fixed a rare \"database is locked\" error when the library opens"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:121
#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:134
#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:160
#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:183
msgid "Updated translations"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:127
msgid ""
"Change a game's artwork from SteamGridDB or your own files, and a tidier "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:129
msgid ""
"Change Artwork, in a game's menu and in fullscreen mode's game options, "
"finds covers, banners, logos, icons and square art on SteamGridDB, page by "
"page, or uses an image file; a picked image shows at once, and Use Original "
"brings the launcher's back"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:130
msgid ""
"When SteamGridDB finds the wrong game for a title, Different Game… lets you "
"choose the right one, which is remembered"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:131
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode switches between kinds of art with the shoulder buttons and "
"loads more images as you reach the end"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:132
msgid ""
"Jump Back In cards are evenly rounded, their art fills them without blurred "
"bands, and Play shows on hover and keyboard focus"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:133
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode's library spaces covers evenly in rows and columns, so the "
"focused cover is never hidden behind its neighbours"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:140
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode in gamescope sessions, where the launcher takes Steam's "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:142
msgid ""
"Play shows a starting screen with the game's art until the game is in front, "
"and offers Cancel after five seconds, so a launch that hangs never leaves "
"you stuck"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:143
msgid ""
"In a gamescope session Steam's own launch window stays hidden; Steam shows "
"only when it needs an answer, such as a sign-in or a cloud conflict"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:144
msgid ""
"The launcher notices within about two seconds that a game handed to Steam, "
"Heroic or Lutris has ended"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:145
msgid ""
"Home opens Steam Big Picture where Steam is installed; the launcher leaves "
"the screen and the controller to Steam until you leave Big Picture"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:146
msgid ""
"The menu's Power lists Suspend, Restart, Power Off and Exit, also in the "
"Flatpak with access outside the sandbox; Exit is left out when the launcher "
"is the session itself"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:147
msgid ""
"The menu's Controls lets you choose which button does what, and Reset to "
"Defaults brings the usual buttons back"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:148
msgid ""
"In a gamescope session started with --steam, the games the launcher starts "
"come to the front, the launcher comes back when they end, and Return in "
"Playing Now goes back to the game"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:149
msgid ""
"Guide opens the menu over a running game, as in Steam: Return, Stop, Home "
"and Library, and the game's windows to switch between when it has more than "
"one"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:150
msgid ""
"Guide + A, the ⋯ button or a right stick click opens Quick Access, over a "
"running game too, including Network and Bluetooth; Guide on its own acts "
"when you let go of it"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:151
msgid ""
"Games handed to Steam, Heroic or Lutris come to the front too and show as "
"playing, with Return instead of Play and a Stop that closes their windows, "
"and Steam's own window shows while it needs an answer"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:152
msgid ""
"Steam starts without its library window in a gamescope session, when the "
"launcher may run commands on the host"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:153
msgid ""
"\"Opening Steam…\" no longer stays on screen when the store launcher never "
"answers"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:154
msgid "The Performance Overlay switch drives MangoApp in a gamescope session"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:155
msgid ""
"The RPM and DEB packages add a \"Pindu launcher\" session to gamescope-"
"session-plus login screens, with Switch to Desktop in the Power menu"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:156
msgid "Games started outside the Flatpak open on the launcher's own display"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:157
msgid "Fullscreen mode can install Steam, Heroic or Lutris from Add a Store"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:158
msgid ""
"Wi-Fi passphrases and Bluetooth PINs are typed with the on-screen keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:159
msgid ""
"Once the launcher starts a game, the controller is the game's: only Guide "
"and Guide + A reach the launcher until Guide, switching back to it or the "
"game ending, so buttons no longer act in the game and the launcher at once"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:166
msgid "A fix for fullscreen mode in virtual machines."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:168
msgid ""
"Fullscreen mode no longer crashes in a virtual machine with 3D acceleration "
"and Venus (virtio-gpu)"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:174
msgid ""
"Release files for ARM (aarch64), a fix for a crash on Steam libraries, and "
"more in the fullscreen Quick Access panel."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:176
msgid ""
"Flatpak, RPM and DEB release files are now built for aarch64 (ARM) as well "
"as x86_64"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:177
msgid "Fixed a crash when importing a Steam library with deeply nested data"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:178
msgid "Windows games use a Proton build made for your machine's architecture"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:179
msgid "Turning on MangoHud now explains when it cannot work inside the sandbox"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:180
msgid ""
"Quick Access in fullscreen mode gains Network, Bluetooth, System Update, "
"Sound Output and Power sections"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:181
msgid ""
"The on-screen keyboard has capitals and symbols, and a dialog for entering "
"passphrases"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:182
msgid "The RPM and DEB packages now depend on GStreamer's good plug-ins"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:189
msgid ""
"Native packages, your own fullscreen style in Preferences, and the start of "
"translations."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:191
msgid ""
"Install Pindu launcher as an RPM on Fedora 45 or a DEB on Debian testing and "
"Ubuntu 26.10, next to the Flatpak"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:192
msgid ""
"Turn your own fullscreen stylesheet on, import it, open its folder or reset "
"it in Preferences, which also lists its problems"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:193
msgid ""
"Without umu-launcher, Windows games now say what is missing and how to "
"install it"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:194
msgid ""
"The focused cover in the first row of the fullscreen library is no longer "
"cut off"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:195
msgid "A first, partial Dutch translation; help translate on Weblate"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:201
msgid ""
"Windows games, and a fullscreen mode for playing from the couch with a "
"controller."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:203
msgid ""
"Add a Windows game from its .exe or installer and play it with Proton, with "
"launch settings and logs for each game"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:204
msgid "Download GE-Proton and Proton-CachyOS builds from Preferences"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:205
msgid ""
"Run native games in the Steam Linux Runtime, and turn on MangoHud or "
"GameMode for a game"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:206
msgid ""
"A fullscreen mode with Home, Library and game pages, an on-screen keyboard "
"for search and a Quick Access panel"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:207
msgid ""
"Fullscreen designs, Ribbon and Panorama, with variants, and your own "
"stylesheet"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:208
msgid ""
"Reduce Motion, four text sizes and a volume for navigation sounds in "
"fullscreen mode"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:209
msgid "Control the desktop window and its menus with a controller"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:210
msgid "SteamGridDB art arrives as soon as you save your key"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:216
msgid "The first release."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:218
msgid ""
"One library for Steam, Heroic, Lutris, Bottles, Faugus, installed apps and "
"games you add yourself"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.tim_van_oudheusden.pindu-launcher.metainfo.xml.in:219
msgid "Collections, favourites, Jump Back In and play history"
